  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40270550",
      "title": "Understanding the useMemo() Hook",
      "sourceHash": "f65e3acdb1541d83bc5d4f3ac25c23da812f30d8495875896808c6f2f304f983",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "Now in this output from the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 8.48,
          "en": "you also see that this calculating if is prime number code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.97,
          "end": 12.09,
          "en": "is output every time we click this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.09,
          "end": 15.3,
          "en": "So this clearly is code that is executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.3,
          "end": 18.363,
          "en": "again, if the counter changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 22.44,
          "en": "And that makes sense because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.44,
          "end": 25.11,
          "en": "it's this isPrime function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.11,
          "end": 27.27,
          "en": "that is called directly inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.27,
          "end": 29.31,
          "en": "of the counter component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.31,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "that is being executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 32.79,
          "en": "whenever this component function changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 34.14,
          "en": "And it's this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.14,
          "end": 36.363,
          "en": "where this log statement is coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.5,
          "end": 41.7,
          "en": "Now, this function is just there for demo purposes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.7,
          "end": 42.6,
          "en": "to be honest.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.6,
          "end": 44.94,
          "en": "But this function does, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.94,
          "end": 48.42,
          "en": "use this initial account value as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.42,
          "end": 51.69,
          "en": "And this value technically only changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.69,
          "end": 55.23,
          "en": "if we enter a new value here and click set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.23,
          "end": 56.97,
          "en": "Though at the moment this doesn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.97,
          "end": 58.8,
          "en": "and we'll fix it later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.8,
          "end": 61.92,
          "en": "But still it's only at this point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 65.34,
          "en": "where a new initial count value will be received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.34,
          "end": 69.12,
          "en": "and isPrime will yield a new result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.12,
          "end": 72.66,
          "en": "Other than that, if initial count does not change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.66,
          "end": 75.57,
          "en": "and if the counter component function is only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.57,
          "end": 79.23,
          "en": "re-executed because the counter state changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.23,
          "end": 83.55,
          "en": "isPrime will always produce the same result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.55,
          "end": 87.48,
          "en": "And that can be a problem if you have a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.48,
          "end": 90.24,
          "en": "that performs a rather complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.24,
          "end": 93.66,
          "en": "and performance intensive calculation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.66,
          "end": 96.6,
          "en": "Which is not necessarily the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.6,
          "end": 100.86,
          "en": "but it's also not a super trivial calculation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.86,
          "end": 104.91,
          "en": "especially if you enter a bigger number in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.91,
          "end": 108.003,
          "en": "like a million, or a trillion, or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.83,
          "end": 113.58,
          "en": "Re-executing all this code all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.58,
          "end": 116.91,
          "en": "even though it will produce the same result as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.91,
          "end": 119.91,
          "en": "is then not very efficient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.91,
          "end": 123.21,
          "en": "And therefore just as you might want to prevent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.21,
          "end": 126.3,
          "en": "component function executions with memo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.3,
          "end": 129.33,
          "en": "you also might want to prevent the execution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.33,
          "end": 131.28,
          "en": "of normal functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.28,
          "end": 134.82,
          "en": "that are called inside of component functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.82,
          "end": 137.67000000000002,
          "en": "unless their input changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.67000000000002,
          "end": 139.38,
          "en": "And React gives us a hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.38,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "that can be used for this scenario and problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 145.62,
          "en": "the useMemo hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.62,
          "end": 148.32,
          "en": "Which is not to be confused with memo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.32,
          "end": 151.17000000000002,
          "en": "memo is wrapped around component functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.17000000000002,
          "end": 153.75,
          "en": "as explained a couple of lectures ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.75,
          "end": 157.82999999999998,
          "en": "useMemo is wrapped around normal functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.82999999999998,
          "end": 161.4,
          "en": "that are executed in component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.4,
          "end": 164.57999999999998,
          "en": "to prevent their execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 167.31,
          "en": "And useMemo should really only be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.31,
          "end": 172.02,
          "en": "if you have a complex calculation that you want to prevent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.02,
          "end": 173.57999999999998,
          "en": "For example, here if we wanna",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.57999999999998,
          "end": 178.57999999999998,
          "en": "prevent isPrime from executing we can call useMemo here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.25,
          "end": 181.39,
          "en": "And then through useMemo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.61,
          "end": 184.92,
          "en": "we pass a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.92,
          "end": 187.68,
          "en": "for example, an anonymous arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.68,
          "end": 190.77,
          "en": "Which then returns the result of the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.77,
          "end": 192.9,
          "en": "that we want to prevent executing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.9,
          "end": 195.33,
          "en": "So it's in this anonymous function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.33,
          "end": 196.923,
          "en": "where we now call isPrime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.761,
          "end": 202.17000000000002,
          "en": "useMemo then also wants a dependencies array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.17000000000002,
          "end": 204.543,
          "en": "just as useCallback wanted it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.38,
          "end": 208.77,
          "en": "And the idea behind useMemo is now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.77,
          "end": 211.82999999999998,
          "en": "that react will now execute this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.82999999999998,
          "end": 213.99,
          "en": "which you pass to useMemo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.99,
          "end": 216.66,
          "en": "So this anonymous arrow function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.66,
          "end": 220.07999999999998,
          "en": "And it will then store the result of this execution,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 220.07999999999998,
          "end": 223.23,
          "en": "so the result of calling isPrime then in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 223.23,
          "end": 227.133,
          "en": "since that's returned in this anonymous function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.27,
          "end": 231.39,
          "en": "And it will only re-execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.39,
          "end": 234.48,
          "en": "if one of those dependencies here changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.48,
          "end": 237.24,
          "en": "So if you have an empty dependencies array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.24,
          "end": 239.49,
          "en": "this will never re-execute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 243.06,
          "en": "because there are no dependencies that could change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 243.06,
          "end": 244.77,
          "en": "But of course here you can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.77,
          "end": 246.87,
          "en": "that I'm already getting a warning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246.87,
          "end": 251.01,
          "en": "because here I should add initial count as a dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.01,
          "end": 255.15,
          "en": "because that is used as a input by isPrime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 255.15,
          "end": 257.95799999999997,
          "en": "And indeed, if initialCount changes isPrime",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 257.95799999999997,
          "end": 260.58,
          "en": "will yield a different result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.58,
          "end": 264.03,
          "en": "and therefore you should add initialCount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 264.03,
          "end": 267.39300000000003,
          "en": "as a value here in this dependencies array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 268.5,
          "end": 271.35,
          "en": "And with that useMemo, we'll now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 271.35,
          "end": 274.89,
          "en": "that in the end isPrime only gets re-executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.89,
          "end": 277.08,
          "en": "if initial count changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 277.08,
          "end": 279.09000000000003,
          "en": "But it will not get executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 279.09000000000003,
          "end": 282.063,
          "en": "if this counter state changed, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 282.99,
          "end": 286.68,
          "en": "So if we save this and we go back and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 286.68,
          "end": 287.73,
          "en": "clear this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 287.73,
          "end": 289.75,
          "en": "you'll see that if I click increment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 291.392,
          "end": 292.68,
          "en": "we no longer get this output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 292.68,
          "end": 295.05,
          "en": "from inside the isPrime function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 295.05,
          "end": 295.953,
          "en": "On the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.841,
          "end": 300.243,
          "en": "if I set a new counter value we do get that output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 301.71,
          "end": 303.63,
          "en": "Now I wanna emphasize though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 303.63,
          "end": 307.41,
          "en": "that you really should not overuse useMemo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 307.41,
          "end": 310.86,
          "en": "You should not start wrapping it around all your functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.86,
          "end": 313.95,
          "en": "because just like Memo, of course it does need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.95,
          "end": 318.36,
          "en": "to perform this extra dependency value comparison.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 318.36,
          "end": 319.8,
          "en": "And if you have a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 319.8,
          "end": 322.95,
          "en": "that for example simply needs to be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 322.95,
          "end": 326.7,
          "en": "on basically every component function, re-execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 326.7,
          "end": 329.58,
          "en": "Adding this extra check doesn't make any sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 329.58,
          "end": 332.493,
          "en": "and instead just cost extra performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 333.57,
          "end": 335.90999999999997,
          "en": "On the other hand here where indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 335.90999999999997,
          "end": 338.64,
          "en": "a lot of executions can be avoided,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 338.64,
          "end": 341.88,
          "en": "and where we potentially execute code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 341.88,
          "end": 343.26,
          "en": "that could take some time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 343.26,
          "end": 347.22,
          "en": "to finish using useMemo makes more sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 347.22,
          "end": 350.1,
          "en": "So just as with memo, you should use it with care.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 350.1,
          "end": 353.31,
          "en": "But if used in the right situations it can help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 353.31,
          "end": 356.613,
          "en": "improve the performance of your react application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}